6. AI/ML applications
==========================

Downscaling Model Architecture Review
The team evaluated deep learning pipelines using U-Transformer architecture and residual diffusion for precipitation downscaling. These models utilize 72 variables to improve accuracy compared to existing generative adversarial networks.

Model Performance and Terminology
Evaluations across 3 flood events revealed that quantile mapping requires seasonal adjustments to avoid overestimation. The team decided to classify the dataset as reference data rather than ground truth to ensure scientific accuracy.

Computational Efficiency and Strategy
The team addressed the computational trade-off required for high-accuracy diffusion models against faster baseline methods. Strategic alignment focused on generating robust statistical samples for extreme precipitation events rather than seeking universal model perfection.

